Ears 8 sketch (2026-10-18): a local, offline sketch for rendering clips; never app code.
Against main at cf67c3f (js/ unchanged since a23153d), applied ON TOP of ears4-sketch.patch:
  git apply tools/ears/sketches/ears4-sketch.patch && git apply tools/ears/sketches/ears8-sketch.patch
The first synthesis's candidates (docs/ears/batch-5.md), behind globalThis.PROTO, each drawing from a
stream of its own so the loop is otherwise unchanged (with PROTO empty the render matches main):
  tunedKick  'on' | 'short' | 'long'   the kick and soft kick land on the key's note, G1-D2 (D# to F#
             take their fifth), with today's sweep and level by ear (K-weighted energy matched at load).
             short: today's shape falling at 180-260 dB/s. long: today's punch, then a tail 7-17 dB down
             ringing at 45-80 dB/s, as loud as fits within +1 dB by ear and +3 dB of today's kick's energy
             under 60 Hz and at 60-120 Hz; choked by the next kick, held in the budget 0.36 s a hit
  subDuck    'on' (half the kick-and-bass loops) | 'force'   the bass channel alone dips 5-9 dB at each
             kick and is back in 0.15-0.25 s
  lateFloor  'on' (3 in 10) | 'force' | 'together' | 'kitFirst' | 'bassFirst'   after a load the kit and
             the bass wait 8-30 s (lateSecs pins it), on a two-bar line, then enter together or 2 bars apart;
             only where chords, melody or texture play from the first second
  padSweep   'on' (3 in 10 sustained-chord loops) | 'force'   a lowpass on the chord layer swings 2-3.5
             octaves up from 450-800 Hz and back, once every 12-28 s, starting closed
  echoTime   'on' | a fraction of the beat   the echo's time per loop: 3/4 (45%), 1 (25%), 1/2, 2/3 (15% each)
  pedalBass  'on' (about 3 in 10 held, pulse, dub and walking basses) | 'force' | 'held' | 'half' |
             'quarter' | 'offbeat'   the bass holds the key's tonic in a rhythm under the chords and now
             and then steps to one neighbor (+2, -2, +1 where the mode has it, or the fifth) and back, in
             the octave nearest the loop's own bass and no longer than its usual note; drift replays the
             original bass's draws, so no other layer's variation moves
  floorDrop  'on' (Ears 1's approved recipe, ported) | 'plus' | 'single' | 'stagger' | 'stutter' | 'long'
             'plus' draws a shape per drop: single 40, stagger 25 (the bass back 1-2 bars after the kick),
             stutter 20 (3-4 short drops, one every 2 or 4 bars), long 15 (10-20 s, or the whole pass in a
             loop of 8 bars or fewer); floorDropRate overrides the 0.35 a pass
The engine logs each load's draws and each drop to globalThis.EARS8_LOG (render2.mjs puts it in its index).

